ork [Data: Entities (2389)]. This device, which may include a modem, router, or bridge, offers a standardized interface for service connections and can integrate multiple functionalities [Data: Entities (2389)]. It is installed and maintained by the provider, with its functionalities potentially limited by them, offering less flexibility to the end-user [Data: Entities (2389)]. This device is essential for connecting internet, telephone, and TV services and acts as the entry point for the provider's network into the residence [Data: Entities (2389)]. The DISPOSITIVO INTERFACE DE REDE connects directly to the REDE INTERNA DO CLIENTE and is considered a type of EQUIPAMENTO DE REDE used for SERVIÇOS DE TELECOMUNICAÇÕES [Data: Relationships (3335, 3339, 3338)]. It is the primary interface connecting the REDE DO PROVEDOR to the customer's internal setup [Data: Relationships (3344)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"User control and troubleshooting capabilities\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The TOMADA AUXILIAR DE DESCONEXÃO provides end-users with the ability to isolate their internal network from the service provider's network [Data: Entities (2390)]. This feature is particularly useful for troubleshooting network problems or performing maintenance without impacting the service provider's infrastructure [Data: Entities (2390)]. By allowing users to isolate their network, it facilitates problem diagnosis and enhances user control over their connection [Data: Entities (2390)]. While beneficial, this component can be overlooked or misused if the user lacks the necessary knowledge to operate it correctly [Data: Entities (2390)]. The TOMADA AUXILIAR DE DESCONEXÃO is utilized for network isolation during testing and temporary service disconnection [Data: Entities (2390)]. It serves as an additional connection point alongside the DISPOSITIVO INTERFACE DE REDE and is valuable for both TESTES and MANUTENÇÃO activities [Data: Relationships (3307, 3347, 3348)]. This component 